{"id": "EUVD-2026-104305", "enisaUuid": "7cbe373a-d5ec-3739-ae02-dfa6e3bd07f4", "description": "sglang-router (sgl-model-gateway) through 0.3.2 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows holders of the data-plane API key to access mesh HA management routes because /ha/* endpoints skip control-plane Admin role checks. Attackers can read cluster topology, write gossiped configuration, change global rate limits, and call POST /ha/shutdown to silently dissolve HA coordination.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T02:48:54", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45006", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45017", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/sgl-model-gateway/src/server.rs#L641-L675", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-router-through-0.3.2-authorization-bypass-via-mesh-ha-management-routes"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112268", "GHSA-q6x7-8366-3wrx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6e21fddf-33c4-38d8-bc0b-6f32103270eb", "product": {"name": "sglang-router", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.3.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c5e97f73-ee52-346d-a828-01918fb797bb", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}